Third-party software
--------------------
Etchwork's own source is MIT. The engine image that `etchwork build` creates
(engine/Dockerfile) downloads and bundles the following, each under its own
licence. They run as separate programs or libraries; their licences apply to
them, not to Etchwork's source.

  KiCad (base image kicad/kicad)   GPL-3.0-or-later   https://www.kicad.org
  Freerouting 2.4.1                GPL-3.0            https://github.com/freerouting/freerouting
  SKiDL 2.3.0                      MIT                https://github.com/devbisme/skidl
  kinet2pcb 1.1.4                  MIT                https://github.com/devbisme/kinet2pcb
  MCP Python SDK 1.30.0            MIT                https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk
  pypdfium2 5.13.0                 Apache-2.0 / BSD-3-Clause (PDFium)
                                                      https://github.com/pypdfium2-team/pypdfium2
  OpenJDK 25 (Debian package)      GPL-2.0 with Classpath Exception

The image applies two small patches at build time: one to kinet2pcb
(engine/Dockerfile) and one to SKiDL (engine/patches/). The KiCad symbol and
footprint libraries are CC-BY-SA-4.0 with an exception for designs made with
them, so boards Etchwork produces are not bound by that licence.

If you redistribute a built engine image, you take on the GPL's obligations
for KiCad and Freerouting, including offering their corresponding source.
